@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il06-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il06-period`
IMPORT `nii-s65-interpretation`
IMPORT `nii-s66-entitlement`
IMPORT `nii-s67-count-of-children`
IMPORT `nii-s68-amount`
IMPORT `nii-il06-published-figures`

-- National Insurance Law, ss 65-68, answered for a family on a day: the child allowance of
-- every person in the family for the month in which the day falls, at the rate in force on
-- the day. s 72 (which months are paid) is not encoded; the answer is the monthly amount the
-- family's facts on that day produce.
--
-- Version 0.2.0 adds a second question, for a family in a month (06-S72; at the end of this
-- module): the allowance for the month, for the children the caller says s 72 pays for in it.
-- It answers the months the day question cannot, such as the month of an 18th birthday that
-- falls on the 1st (s 72(a) pays that month; on every day of it the child is 18).
--
-- Order of the answer:
--   1. a day before 1 May 2015 is declined (nii-il06-period.l4);
--   2. facts that cannot describe a case are returned as a problem (LEFT), for the caller to
--      fix (phrasebook 11.4);
--   3. every child's count is settled, through s 67(a), so that any refusal in s 67 reaches
--      the caller before an answer is handed back (phrasebook 11.8);
--   4. one answer per person, in the order of the family's list (RIGHT).

§ `A family on a day — the answer`

§§ `Facts that cannot describe a case`

GIVEN `the names` IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no name repeats in` `the names` MEANS
    count (nub `the names`) EQUALS count `the names`

-- The checks a family on a day and a family in a month share, in the order they are made. The
-- check on a child's birth (and, for a month, age) comes fourth and differs between the two, so
-- it is an argument, reached only if the first three pass.
-- Version 0.2.0 (06-F5): an absence that ended before the day is reported, not read. Before,
-- such an absence was measured as the child's absence on the day, so a child who had come back
-- was treated as abroad, with no diagnostic (INDEPENDENT-FINDINGS.md, finding 5). The return day
-- itself is not "before the day": an absence that ends on the day asked about is in progress on it.
GIVEN `the family`                       IS A `A family on a day`
      `the problem with a child's birth` IS A MAYBE `A problem with the facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE `A problem with the facts`
`the first problem with the facts of` `the family` `, the check on births being` `the problem with a child's birth` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `no name repeats in` (map (GIVEN p YIELD p's `name`) `the persons`)
           THEN JUST `two persons have the same name`
           IF any (GIVEN c YIELD any (GIVEN e YIELD null (`the persons named` (e's `name of the person`) `in` `the family`)) (c's `parents`)) `the children`
           THEN JUST `a child's record names a parent who is not among the persons`
           IF NOT `no name repeats in` (map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `name`) `the children`)
           THEN JUST `two children have the same name`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `the problem with a child's birth`
               WHEN JUST `the problem` THEN JUST `the problem`
               WHEN NOTHING
               THEN BRANCH IF any `an absence that cannot be` `the children`
                           THEN JUST `an absence from Israel begins after the day, or ends before it begins`
                           IF any `an absence that ended before the day` `the children`
                           THEN JUST `an absence from Israel ended before the day`
                           OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the persons`  MEANS `the family`'s `the persons`
        `the children` MEANS `the family`'s `the children`
        `the day`      MEANS `the family`'s `the day`
        `an absence that cannot be` c MEANS
            CONSIDER c's `absence from Israel`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST a  THEN     a's `the day the child left Israel` GREATER THAN `the day`
                              OR (CONSIDER a's `the day the child returned to Israel`
                                  WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                                  WHEN JUST r  THEN r LESS THAN a's `the day the child left Israel`)
        `an absence that ended before the day` c MEANS
            CONSIDER c's `absence from Israel`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST a  THEN CONSIDER a's `the day the child returned to Israel`
                              WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                              WHEN JUST r  THEN r LESS THAN `the day`

-- The fourth check, for the question asked (version 0.2.0): for the day, a child born after it;
-- for the month s 72 pays, a listed child born after the month, or 18 before it began (s 72
-- cannot pay for either in that month; nii-s65-interpretation.l4, the month's age limb).
GIVEN `the question` IS A `The question asked of a family on a day`
      `the family`   IS A `A family on a day`
GIVETH A MAYBE `A problem with the facts`
`a problem with the facts, asked` `the question` `, of` `the family` MEANS
    `the first problem with the facts of` `the family` `, the check on births being`
        (CONSIDER `the question`
         WHEN `the allowance on the family's day`
         THEN IF   any (GIVEN c YIELD c's `date of birth` GREATER THAN `the day`) `the children`
              THEN JUST `a child is born after the day`
              ELSE NOTHING
         WHEN `the allowance for the month of the family's day, for the children section 72 pays for in it`
         THEN BRANCH IF any (GIVEN c YIELD c's `date of birth` GREATER THAN `the last day of the month of` `the day`) `the children`
                     THEN JUST `a child said to be paid for in the month is born after the month`
                     IF any (GIVEN c YIELD `the 18th anniversary of the birth of` c LESS THAN `the first day of the month of` `the day`) `the children`
                     THEN JUST `a child said to be paid for in the month reached 18 before the month began`
                     OTHERWISE NOTHING)
    WHERE
        `the day`      MEANS `the family`'s `the day`
        `the children` MEANS `the family`'s `the children`

GIVEN `the family` IS A `A family on a day`
GIVETH A MAYBE `A problem with the facts`
`a problem with the facts of` `the family` MEANS
    `a problem with the facts, asked` `the allowance on the family's day` `, of` `the family`

§§ `The answer, at basic amounts the caller supplies`

@ref National Insurance Law s 67(a) (source line 817): the counts of this model break it only if the construction in nii-s67-count-of-children.l4 is wrong
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the counts this model computed break section 67(a), which its construction is meant to rule out` MEANS
    REFUSE "the counts this model computed break section 67(a), which its construction is meant to rule out"

-- Version 0.2.0: asked of the day or of the month s 72 pays (nii-il06-nouns.l4, `The question
-- asked of a family on a day`); the day's form, as before, follows it.
@ref National Insurance Law ss 65-68 (source lines 799-834)
GIVEN `the question` IS A `The question asked of a family on a day`
      `the family`   IS A `A family on a day`
      `the amounts`  IS A `The basic amounts for the child allowance`
GIVETH AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
`the child allowance of each person, asked` `the question` `, in` `the family` `, at` `the amounts` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the deposited text of sections 65 to 68 was in force on` (`the family`'s `the day`)
           THEN `this model answers days from 1 May 2015, when sections 1 and 68 took their present wording; the text in force before then is not in its sources`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `a problem with the facts, asked` `the question` `, of` `the family`
               WHEN JUST `the problem` THEN LEFT `the problem`
               WHEN NOTHING
               THEN IF   `s 67(a) — no child is counted with more than one insured parent, asked` `the question` `, in` `the family`
                    THEN RIGHT (map `the answer for` (`the family`'s `the persons`))
                    ELSE `the counts this model computed break section 67(a), which its construction is meant to rule out`
    WHERE
        `the answer for` p MEANS
            `A person's child allowance for the month` WITH
                `name of the person` IS p's `name`
                `the answer`         IS `s 68 — the child allowance, asked` `the question` `, in` `the family` `, at` `the amounts` `, of` p

@ref National Insurance Law ss 65-68 (source lines 799-834)
GIVEN `the family`  IS A `A family on a day`
      `the amounts` IS A `The basic amounts for the child allowance`
GIVETH AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
`the child allowance of each person, in` `the family` `, at` `the amounts` MEANS
    `the child allowance of each person, asked` `the allowance on the family's day` `, in` `the family` `, at` `the amounts`

§§ `The answer, at the basic amounts the Institute published`

@ref National Insurance Law ss 65-68; the basic amounts from nii-il06-published-figures.l4 (not encoded law)
GIVEN `the family` IS A `A family on a day`
GIVETH AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
`the child allowance of each person, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the day, in` `the family` MEANS
    `the child allowance of each person, in` `the family` `, at` (`the basic amounts for the child allowance the Institute published for` (`the family`'s `the day`))

-- The family's total for the month, before rounding: the sum of every person's total.
GIVEN `the answers` IS A LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the family's total, before rounding, of` `the answers` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN a YIELD `the total, before rounding, of` (a's `the answer`)) `the answers`)

§ `A family in a month — the answer, for the children section 72 pays for`

-- Version 0.2.0 (06-S72). s 72(a) pays the allowance from the 1st of the month in which
-- entitlement arose, if it arose by the 15th, and to the last day of the month in which it
-- ceased. So in the month of an 18th birthday the child is paid for although, from the birthday
-- on, the child is not under 18; and in the month of a birth by the 15th the child is paid for
-- although, before the birth, there is no child. The day question above cannot answer such a
-- month where no single day of it finds every child paid for both born and under 18: an 18th
-- birthday on the 1st, or one on or before the birth of another child paid for in the month.
-- src:854 | (א) נוצרה זכאות לקצבת ילדים עד 15 בחודש פלוני, תשולם הקצבה החל ב־1 באותו חודש; נוצרה הזכאות אחרי 15 בחודש פלוני, תשולם הקצבה החל ב־1 בחודש שלאחריו; תשלום הקצבה יסתיים ביום האחרון של החודש שבו נפסקה הזכאות.
--
-- WHAT THIS QUESTION TAKES FROM THE CALLER. Which children s 72 pays for in the month (row IL-08
-- encodes s 72; this row does not). Every other fact is as it stands on the day the record names.
--
-- HOW IT IS ANSWERED. Not by a second composition: the month is put as a family on its day
-- (`the family in a month, on its day:`, nii-s65-interpretation.l4), and the rules of ss 65-68
-- above and in their modules are asked `the allowance for the month of the family's day, …`
-- instead of `the allowance on the family's day`. That changes two things only: s 65's age limb
-- (a listed child whose 18th birthday is on or after the month's first day, and who is born by its
-- last, is within it for the month), and the fourth check on the facts (a listed child outside
-- that is a problem with the facts, not a child left out). The count for the month is the listed
-- children s 67 places with the parent, eldest first (fork F4); a child paid for in the month of
-- its 18th birthday keeps its place and counts for s 68(c)'s "three or more children" (fork F19).

@ref National Insurance Law ss 65-68 (source lines 799-834), s 72(a) (source line 854) as the caller applies it
GIVEN `the family`  IS A `A family in a month`
          @desc a day in the month (on which every fact but the children's dates of birth stands), the persons, and the children s 72 pays for in that month
      `the amounts` IS A `The basic amounts for the child allowance`
          @desc the three basic amounts of s 1 "the basic amount" paragraph (2) in force in the month
GIVETH AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
`the child allowance of each person for the month, for the children section 72 pays for, in` `the family` `, at` `the amounts` MEANS
    `the child allowance of each person, asked` `the allowance for the month of the family's day, for the children section 72 pays for in it`
        `, in` (`the family in a month, on its day:` `the family`) `, at` `the amounts`

-- The basic amounts change only on 1 January (s 1, updating clause (3), line 197), so the
-- Institute's figures for the month's first day are its figures for every day of the month.
@ref National Insurance Law ss 65-68, s 72(a) as the caller applies it; the basic amounts from nii-il06-published-figures.l4 (not encoded law)
GIVEN `the family` IS A `A family in a month`
          @desc a day in the month (on which every fact but the children's dates of birth stands), the persons, and the children s 72 pays for in that month
GIVETH AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` (LIST OF `A person's child allowance for the month`)
`the child allowance of each person for the month, for the children section 72 pays for, at the basic amounts the Institute published for the month, in` `the family` MEANS
    `the child allowance of each person for the month, for the children section 72 pays for, in` `the family` `, at`
        (`the basic amounts for the child allowance the Institute published for` (`the first day of the month of` (`the family`'s `a day in the month, on which the facts stand`)))
